{
  "width": 7300,
  "height": 3760,
  "intro": "Every path from a key press to the speakers, read left to right. Pick an area to zoom in, or follow the signal with Next.",
  "zones": [
    {
      "id": "play",
      "title": "Play",
      "blurb": "Everything you play the instrument with: the keys on screen and on your computer, MIDI gear, the wheels, the XY pad, Live FX and Wi-Fi sync. The microphone and audio files feed the sampler.",
      "x": 40,
      "y": 250,
      "w": 490,
      "h": 3010
    },
    {
      "id": "notes",
      "title": "Notes & time",
      "blurb": "What happens to a note before a machine plays it — scale, chords, the arpeggiator — and the clock that keeps every machine in time.",
      "x": 620,
      "y": 250,
      "w": 550,
      "h": 3010
    },
    {
      "id": "machines",
      "title": "Machines & sound sources",
      "blurb": "What makes the sound: the synth with its sequencers, the drum machine and the sampler. Each ends in its own bus.",
      "x": 1220,
      "y": 250,
      "w": 2580,
      "h": 3010
    },
    {
      "id": "fx",
      "title": "FX rack",
      "blurb": "Three insert chains, one per bus, lined up by effect. A bypassed effect is disconnected, so it costs nothing.",
      "x": 3830,
      "y": 250,
      "w": 1870,
      "h": 3010
    },
    {
      "id": "master",
      "title": "Master & output",
      "blurb": "The three buses sum, pass the DJ FILTER, the MASTER COMP and the MASTER VOL, and leave as stereo.",
      "x": 5740,
      "y": 250,
      "w": 1520,
      "h": 3010
    },
    {
      "id": "synth",
      "parent": "machines",
      "title": "Synth",
      "blurb": "Notes from the keys, the arpeggiator or the step sequencer go to the voice allocator, which plays up to eight copies of the synth voice.",
      "x": 1232,
      "y": 262,
      "w": 2556,
      "h": 1384
    },
    {
      "id": "drums",
      "parent": "machines",
      "title": "Drums",
      "blurb": "The drum machine: eight synthesized drum tracks, each through its own channel strip, into the drum bus.",
      "x": 1232,
      "y": 1694,
      "w": 2556,
      "h": 758
    },
    {
      "id": "sampler",
      "parent": "machines",
      "title": "Sampler",
      "blurb": "The sampler machine: eight slots of recorded sound, each through its own channel strip, into the sampler bus.",
      "x": 1232,
      "y": 2496,
      "w": 2556,
      "h": 752
    },
    {
      "id": "play-keys",
      "parent": "play",
      "title": "Keyboards & MIDI",
      "blurb": "The on-screen keys, the computer keyboard and MIDI IN all send notes the same way. MIDI also brings pitch bend, the mod wheel, volume, sustain and its clock; channel 10 plays the sampler pads.",
      "x": 48,
      "y": 278,
      "w": 474,
      "h": 674
    },
    {
      "id": "play-ctl",
      "parent": "play",
      "title": "Controllers & sync",
      "blurb": "The wheels bend the pitch and add modulation. The XY pad and Live FX turn knobs for you (purple wires). Wi-Fi sync locks the clock to another device.",
      "x": 48,
      "y": 952,
      "w": 474,
      "h": 744
    },
    {
      "id": "play-in",
      "parent": "play",
      "title": "Sound in",
      "blurb": "The microphone records into the sample studio and is never heard live. Audio files load straight into a sampler slot.",
      "x": 48,
      "y": 2588,
      "w": 474,
      "h": 322
    },
    {
      "id": "notes-keys",
      "parent": "notes",
      "title": "Key, chord & arpeggiator",
      "blurb": "KEY quantizes what you play to a scale; CHORD MEMORY turns one key into a chord. While the ARPEGGIATOR is on it takes over the live keys and plays them as a pattern.",
      "x": 628,
      "y": 278,
      "w": 534,
      "h": 372
    },
    {
      "id": "notes-clock",
      "parent": "notes",
      "title": "Clock, song & automation",
      "blurb": "The CLOCK ticks in 16ths and drives every machine. SYNC follows or leads MIDI or a Wi-Fi peer; ARRANGEMENT chains banks into a song. The PARAMETER BUS is how anything that turns a knob reaches it.",
      "x": 628,
      "y": 648,
      "w": 534,
      "h": 948
    },
    {
      "id": "notes-studio",
      "parent": "notes",
      "title": "Sample studio",
      "blurb": "Edits a recording before it becomes a sampler slot: crop, normalize, fade, filter, pitch, time-stretch, scratch, chop, and a vocoder that lets a voice take shape the clip. Its clip preview goes straight to the output.",
      "x": 628,
      "y": 2588,
      "w": 534,
      "h": 252
    },
    {
      "id": "seqs",
      "parent": "synth",
      "title": "Sequencers & polyphony",
      "blurb": "The STEP SEQUENCER plays four tracks of notes; the MOTION SEQUENCER automates knobs. POLYPHONY hands each note to a free voice, with unison, glide and voice stealing.",
      "x": 1258,
      "y": 288,
      "w": 864,
      "h": 650
    },
    {
      "id": "voice",
      "parent": "synth",
      "title": "Synth voice",
      "blurb": "One voice, drawn in full: OSC 1, OSC 2 (with FM and sync), SUB and NOISE mix into the FILTER, then the VCA opened by the AMP ENV. Eight of these play at once.",
      "x": 2150,
      "y": 262,
      "w": 1540,
      "h": 808
    },
    {
      "id": "mod",
      "parent": "synth",
      "title": "Modulation",
      "blurb": "The control signals that move the voice: two LFOs, the 6-row MOD MATRIX, the S&H RANDOM source, the envelopes and your bend and mod wheels, all on one MOD BUS.",
      "x": 2150,
      "y": 1030,
      "w": 1540,
      "h": 602
    },
    {
      "id": "drum-machine",
      "parent": "drums",
      "title": "Drum machine",
      "blurb": "Eight tracks of steps trigger eight drum voices, picked from 13 synthesized models and 7 kits. Each hit also tells the DUCK effects when to dip.",
      "x": 1258,
      "y": 1718,
      "w": 854,
      "h": 682
    },
    {
      "id": "drum-channel",
      "parent": "drums",
      "title": "Drum channel",
      "blurb": "Every drum track has its own DRIVE, TONE, LEVEL and PAN, then all eight sum on the DRUM BUS. The lane MUTE and SOLO silence the pattern ahead of each channel, so an audition still plays.",
      "x": 2160,
      "y": 1897,
      "w": 1628,
      "h": 260
    },
    {
      "id": "sampler-machine",
      "parent": "sampler",
      "title": "Sampler pads",
      "blurb": "Eight slots, each playing a one-shot recording, triggered by the sampler steps or MIDI channel 10. Slots fill from a file, the studio, or by rendering the synth.",
      "x": 1258,
      "y": 2508,
      "w": 854,
      "h": 682
    },
    {
      "id": "sampler-channel",
      "parent": "sampler",
      "title": "Sampler channel",
      "blurb": "Each slot plays a window of its recording at a pitch, shaped by a hit envelope, a tone filter, its level and pan, then sums on the SAMPLER BUS. The lane MUTE and SOLO silence the pattern ahead of each channel, so an audition or a MIDI pad still plays.",
      "x": 2160,
      "y": 2687,
      "w": 1628,
      "h": 260
    },
    {
      "id": "fx-synth",
      "parent": "fx",
      "title": "Synth effects",
      "blurb": "The full chain: EQ, DIRT, WAH, PHASER, FLANGER, CHORUS, DELAY, REVERB, DUCK and SYNTH PAN, in that order.",
      "x": 3850,
      "y": 435,
      "w": 1836,
      "h": 336
    },
    {
      "id": "fx-inserts",
      "parent": "fx",
      "title": "How the insert chains work",
      "blurb": "The rules every chain shares: the fixed order, dry/wet crossfades, what each bus has and lacks, and how DUCK listens to drum hits instead of audio.",
      "x": 3868,
      "y": 1098,
      "w": 1474,
      "h": 232
    },
    {
      "id": "fx-drum",
      "parent": "fx",
      "title": "Drum effects",
      "blurb": "EQ, the FET COMP, PHASER, DELAY and REVERB. The drums are never ducked.",
      "x": 3850,
      "y": 1852,
      "w": 1836,
      "h": 336
    },
    {
      "id": "fx-sampler",
      "parent": "fx",
      "title": "Sampler effects",
      "blurb": "EQ, DIRT, PHASER, FLANGER, CHORUS, DELAY, REVERB and DUCK.",
      "x": 3850,
      "y": 2642,
      "w": 1836,
      "h": 336
    },
    {
      "id": "master-chain",
      "parent": "master",
      "title": "Master chain",
      "blurb": "PRE-MASTER sum → DJ FILTER → MASTER COMP → MASTER VOL → LIMITER → OUTPUT → L / R. The SCOPE taps before the volume and RECORD / EXPORT after the limiter; the metronome and clip preview go straight out.",
      "x": 5740,
      "y": 1188,
      "w": 1512,
      "h": 912
    },
    {
      "id": "master-stereo",
      "parent": "master",
      "title": "Where the signal turns stereo",
      "blurb": "The synth is mono until SPREAD, CHORUS, PING PONG, REVERB or SYNTH PAN; drums and sampler turn stereo at each channel's PAN.",
      "x": 5848,
      "y": 288,
      "w": 1394,
      "h": 232
    },
    {
      "id": "master-offpath",
      "parent": "master",
      "title": "Not on the audio path",
      "blurb": "Things that change the sound without being an effect: TAPE STOP, STUTTER, FILL, the microphone and RENDER TO SAMPLER.",
      "x": 5848,
      "y": 2318,
      "w": 1394,
      "h": 232
    },
    {
      "id": "legend",
      "title": "Legend",
      "blurb": "How to read the map: what each wire carries, what the symbols mean, and which colour is which section.",
      "x": 40,
      "y": 3310,
      "w": 7220,
      "h": 410
    },
    {
      "id": "legend-wires",
      "parent": "legend",
      "title": "Wires",
      "blurb": "The colour and line of a wire say what travels on it: audio (single = mono, double = stereo), notes, velocity, modulation, clock, drum hits, automation and sample data.",
      "x": 40,
      "y": 3310,
      "w": 1760,
      "h": 410
    },
    {
      "id": "legend-symbols",
      "parent": "legend",
      "title": "Symbols",
      "blurb": "Σ adds signals, × multiplies them, the triangle is the VCA. Dashed frames repeat per voice or track; a lettered tag continues a wire elsewhere.",
      "x": 1810,
      "y": 3310,
      "w": 1720,
      "h": 410
    },
    {
      "id": "legend-sections",
      "parent": "legend",
      "title": "Section colours",
      "blurb": "The colour strip on every block says which section it belongs to.",
      "x": 3530,
      "y": 3310,
      "w": 840,
      "h": 410
    }
  ],
